---
const publicSources = [
  ['SEC EDGAR', 'https://www.sec.gov/search-filings', 'Selected company disclosures in Form 8-K. Includes material cybersecurity filings and verified voluntary disclosures.'],
  ['HHS Office for Civil Rights', 'https://ocrportal.hhs.gov/ocr/breach/breach_report_hip.jsf', 'Healthcare hacking and IT incidents from the 500-plus-person public listing. Submission date, not incident date.'],
  ['FBI Internet Crime Complaint Center', 'https://www.ic3.gov/CSA/', 'Selected cyber alerts and public warnings. An alert is not proof that a breach occurred.'],
  ['U.S. Department of Justice', 'https://www.justice.gov/criminal/computer-crime-and-intellectual-property-section-ccips-news', 'Official cyber enforcement announcements. Charged allegations are not findings of guilt.'],
  ['CISA Advisories', 'https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories', 'Federal threat campaigns and defensive advisories.'],
  ['CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities', 'https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog', 'Vulnerabilities CISA has identified as exploited. Not an incident count.'],
  ['California DOJ', 'https://oag.ca.gov/privacy/databreach/list', 'State breach notices and original notification samples.'],
  ['Washington Attorney General', 'https://www.atg.wa.gov/data-breach-notifications', 'Washington breach notices, with direct links where available.'],
  ['Oregon DOJ', 'https://justice.oregon.gov/consumer/databreach/', 'Oregon breach records and reported dates.'],
  ['Vermont Attorney General', 'https://ago.vermont.gov/categories/security-breach-notices', 'Vermont breach reports and reporting dates.'],
  ['Iowa Attorney General', 'https://www.iowaattorneygeneral.gov/for-consumers/security-breach-notifications/2026-security-breach-notification', 'Iowa notices with original documents.'],
  ['Massachusetts Consumer Affairs', 'https://www.mass.gov/doc/data-breach-report-2026/download', 'Selected notices involving at least 500 Massachusetts residents in the state report.'],
];
const reporting = [
  ['Associated Press','https://apnews.com/'], ['Reuters','https://www.reuters.com/'], ['NBC News','https://www.nbcnews.com/'],
  ['ABC News','https://abcnews.com/'], ['The Washington Post','https://www.washingtonpost.com/'],
  ['BleepingComputer','https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/'], ['TechCrunch','https://techcrunch.com/'],
  ['Becker’s Hospital Review','https://www.beckershospitalreview.com/'],
];
---
<section id="cyber-source-bank" class="cyber-source-bank" aria-labelledby="cyber-source-bank-title">
  <h2 id="cyber-source-bank-title">Sources and coverage</h2>
  <div class="cyber-source-bank__refresh" data-ticker-refresh aria-label="Refresh schedule">
    <p><strong>Checks every 5 minutes</strong> while this tab is open. DAL-X checks news sources about every 15 minutes and official sources about every 60 minutes, then shares one cached result with all visitors.</p>
    <p data-ticker-status aria-live="polite">Loading public reports…</p>
    <p data-ticker-next></p>
  </div>
  <noscript><style>.cyber-source-bank [data-ticker-status]{display:none}</style></noscript>
  <p>The ticker shows recent public notices, filings, and advisories. Reviewed incidents are presented separately. The archive is not a complete census of U.S. cyber incidents. Automatic ticker checks cover CISA advisories and KEV, FBI IC3 alerts, HHS, and seven state registries listed under State source coverage. SEC, DOJ, the periodic state sources, and reviewed national reporting are updated separately. The archive combines a published history with recent reports from the automatic checks. Reviewed national stories are published separately.</p>
  <details>
    <summary>Automatic source status</summary>
    <p>“Current” means DAL-X reached the source and read its records. It does not mean the publisher posted a new report. Dates below are the latest records the publisher returned, not attack dates.</p>
    <ul class="cyber-source-bank__health" data-source-health><li>Waiting for a publisher check.</li></ul>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>Federal sources and original state sources</summary>
    <ul>{publicSources.map(([name, url, scope]) => <li><a href={url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{name}</a><span>{scope}</span></li>)}</ul>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>How breaking reports are captured</summary>
    <p>Breaking reports are U.S. cyber incident headlines from national, local, and specialist news outlets, captured within about 15 minutes of publication. DAL-X stores only the headline, outlet, time, and link. Coverage of the same story from several outlets is grouped into one entry. These are unreviewed news reports, not confirmed incidents. Stories that DAL-X verifies move into the reviewed incidents, labeled as a national cyber incident or AI agent security case.</p>
    <p>News sources: Google News U.S. edition (filtered to reputable national outlets and U.S. local newsrooms), BleepingComputer, The Record, SecurityWeek, and CyberScoop.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>How we classify AI agent security reports</summary>
    <p>An AI agent must be central to what happened. A reviewed incident requires evidence that an agent was used, misused, or failed in a real environment. We look for a primary disclosure or two independent reports, describe the scope that was confirmed, and distinguish internal control failures from customer breaches.</p>
    <p>Advisories and disclosed vulnerabilities stay labeled as such. A CVE, a lab demonstration, or a malicious package without a confirmed victim does not establish a real-world incident. We use <a href="https://blueradius.io/research/ai-agent-incident-tracker" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BlueRadius Research</a> to find leads, then check the underlying evidence.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>National and specialist reporting used for reviewed incidents</summary>
    <p>Reporting helps identify incidents. Where available, reviewed entries also link to an original company, agency, court, or regulator disclosure. The site does not automatically republish publisher feeds.</p>
    <ul>{reporting.map(([name,url]) => <li><a href={url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{name}</a></li>)}</ul>
  </details>
</section>
<style>
.cyber-source-bank{margin-block:2.5rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere;scroll-margin-top:1rem}
.cyber-source-bank h2{font-size:clamp(1.8rem,5vw,3rem);line-height:1.1}
.cyber-source-bank p{max-width:74ch;color:#cdc2b9;line-height:1.55;margin:.8rem 0}
.cyber-source-bank__refresh{font-size:.85rem}
.cyber-source-bank__refresh p{margin:.2rem 0}
.cyber-source-bank details{border-block-end:1px solid #493a32}
.cyber-source-bank summary{min-height:44px;padding:.7rem 0;cursor:pointer;color:#f1a373}
.cyber-source-bank ul{padding:0 0 1rem;list-style:none;display:grid;gap:.75rem}
.cyber-source-bank span{display:block;font-size:.85rem;color:#cdc2b9}
.cyber-source-bank a{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-height:44px;color:#f4f0ec;text-decoration:underline}
</style>
